            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous rhizotomy of the articular nerve of Luschka for low back and sciatic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>67-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The results of percutaneous facet rhizotomy for the treatment of low back and sciatic pain in 30 patients are reported. Satisfactory results were obtained in 76% of cases. No complications were found. This procedure should be tried in every patient with low back and extremity pain and no major neurological deficit before resorting to laminectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
